<com:TContent ID="body" >

<h1>TInlineFrame</h1>
<com:DocLink ClassPath="Prado.Web.UI.WebControls.TInlineFrame" />

<p class="block-content">
<tt>TInlineFrame</tt> displays an inline frame (&lt;iframe&gt;) on a Web page. The location of the frame content is specified by the <tt>FrameUrl</tt> property.
</p>
<p class="block-content">
<tt>Width</tt> and <tt>Height</tt> size the frame in pixels and render the attributes of
the same name. The control also carries the <tt>CssClass</tt> and <tt>Style</tt>
properties of a web control, and its <tt>Attributes</tt> collection reaches any other
attribute an <tt>&lt;iframe&gt;</tt> accepts.
</p>

<com:TTextHighlighter Language="prado" CssClass="source block-content">
&lt;com:TInlineFrame FrameUrl="?page=Home" Width="600" Height="400"
    Attributes.loading="lazy" Attributes.title="Embedded home page" /&gt;
</com:TTextHighlighter>

<h2>Six properties to avoid</h2>

<p class="block-content">
The control predates HTML5, which dropped the presentational attributes of the
<tt>&lt;iframe&gt;</tt> element. Six properties still write those attributes, and the
framework marks all six deprecated. They continue to render, so existing pages keep
working, and CSS replaces every one of them.
</p>

<table class="parameters">
<tr><th>Deprecated property</th><th>Writes</th><th>Use instead</th></tr>
<tr>
	<td><tt>Align</tt></td>
	<td><tt>align</tt></td>
	<td>The CSS <tt>float</tt> or <tt>vertical-align</tt> declaration.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
	<td><tt>ScrollBars</tt></td>
	<td><tt>scrolling</tt></td>
	<td>The CSS <tt>overflow</tt> declaration inside the framed document.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
	<td><tt>ShowBorder</tt></td>
	<td><tt>frameborder</tt></td>
	<td>The CSS <tt>border</tt> declaration, set to <tt>none</tt>.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
	<td><tt>MarginWidth</tt>, <tt>MarginHeight</tt></td>
	<td><tt>marginwidth</tt>, <tt>marginheight</tt></td>
	<td>The CSS <tt>margin</tt> or <tt>padding</tt> declaration inside the framed document.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
	<td><tt>DescriptionUrl</tt></td>
	<td><tt>longdesc</tt></td>
	<td>An ARIA attribute such as <tt>aria-describedby</tt>.</td>
</tr>
</table>

<h2>Framing another site</h2>

<p class="block-content">
A frame that loads a document from elsewhere gives that document a place in the page. The
<tt>sandbox</tt> attribute limits what the framed document may do, and the
<tt>Attributes</tt> collection sets it. A frame with no <tt>title</tt> attribute is
unlabeled for a screen reader, so a page that frames content should set one.
</p>

